    "semantics":  [
                      "TC SpellInfo applies seal/hand/aura/judgement exclusivity per caster, not one aura globally across all paladins.",
                      "TC SpellMgr normalizes first ranks, expands subgroups, gives a shared nested subgroup precedence, and uses actual strongest absolute amount for matching SAME_EFFECT aura types.",
                      "SAME_EFFECT does not itself remove the other aura in TC Aura.CanStackWith. Category overlap is not universal whole-buff equivalence.",
                      "Actual database rows and SpellInfo aura effects are required. A rule enum alone cannot prove a realm category.",
                      "The pinned AC headers, not the inconsistent current AC wiki flag table, define the numeric rules used for these pinned SQL rows."
                  ],
    "boundaries":  [
                       "Reference TC/AC commits do not identify the user realm, server build, configured world database, custom scripts or active ranks/talents.",
                       "No current IDA call, client function execution, executable/IDB mutation, SQL execution or local project build/test was performed.",
                       "The new TC recursive tree-listing provider refusal remains separately preserved and unexecuted; known-path source reads are not a recovered tree listing.",
                       "No original-client effective aura amount or proc-adjusted cast time is established by these server source files.",
                       "Absence of a particular direct spell ID in these group rows does not exclude implementation through rank chains, other effects, scripts or actual realm data."
                   ]
}
